1
00:00:00,120 --> 00:00:03,021
The One who made every ocean gasped two words

2
00:00:03,141 --> 00:00:05,562
on a cross: I thirst.

3
00:00:06,783 --> 00:00:07,743
Psalm twenty-two.

4
00:00:08,644 --> 00:00:11,165
David wrote it in the first person, but he

5
00:00:11,185 --> 00:00:12,845
was picturing someone else's death.

6
00:00:14,046 --> 00:00:17,647
Watch the body give out: "My strength is dried

7
00:00:17,727 --> 00:00:21,069
up like a potsherd; and my tongue cleaveth

8
00:00:21,309 --> 00:00:25,070
to my jaws; and thou hast brought me into the

9
00:00:25,170 --> 00:00:28,212
dust of death." Dried clay; a tongue stuck

10
00:00:28,292 --> 00:00:31,453
fast; a man sinking into the dust of death.

11
00:00:32,613 --> 00:00:35,915
Then John records the dying Jesus' cry: "I

12
00:00:36,035 --> 00:00:38,536
thirst." Psalm twenty-two does not foretell

13
00:00:38,576 --> 00:00:41,457
that cry, it paints the thirst behind it,

14
00:00:41,977 --> 00:00:43,898
a thousand years before He felt it.

15
00:00:45,099 --> 00:00:47,560
The One who offers the world living water hung

16
00:00:47,620 --> 00:00:49,360
there dry, in your place.

17
00:00:50,441 --> 00:00:52,662
Bring Him your thirst, and drink.

18
00:00:53,822 --> 00:00:55,583
That water is Himself.
